From 95e740ef08b03cb5b3c5b6c7e185083f25b8c7d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: radxa <radxa@radxa-cubie-a7a>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 09:03:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] pco: add the F16SOP packed-half instruction encodings

F16SOP was the missing piece of the mediump story: the vendor GLES compiler lowers
mediump arithmetic to packed half-precision F16SOP (two half ops per instruction),
which is why its shaders need ~half the instruction groups of pco on the bump
(17 vs 33) and effect2d-conv9 (31 vs 58) fragment shaders.

Add the encoding tables derived from the vendor's own output (vendor-usc oracle):
F_SOP_SEL (add/min/max, sub = add+negate), F_SOP_LIT (power-of-two literal codes
0x40+k / 0x4a-k and the 0x62 constant-pool marker), the I_MAIN payload pieces and
fields for bytes 1-23 (negate/abs modifiers, literal code), and five multi-byte
instruction structs: I_F16SOP_EXPR, I_F16SOP_MUL, I_F16SOP_MUL_TEMP, I_F16SOP_MAD,
I_F16SOP_LIT.  pco_ops.py gains O_F16SOP and the OM_SOP_OP modifier; pco_map.py
maps it to F_SOP_SEL and provides the SOPEXPR encode map.

Validated offline against the captured vendor bytes: 32/32 byte checks pass
(lengths, every non-TODO byte for ADD/SUB/ABS/MIN/MAX/MUL/MUL_TEMP/MAD and
literals 1.0/2.0/0.5/-1.0, and the op/neg/abs field deltas).  The argument/
register encoding in bytes 11-21 and the form selection are explicit TODOs
(raw argNN fields) and are the next step.  No behaviour change yet: the offline
harness still reports the math FS at 280 B / 26 groups and the 17-group gate
passes on this tree.
